## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end Azure-native, multi-tenant data platform design under regulatory constraints with real-time processing, governance, security, disaster recovery, and cost discipline.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant isolation and per-tenant policy enforcement
- EU data residency with bring-your-own-key (BYOK) encryption
- Real-time event processing using Durable Functions
- Data governance with Purview and token-based sharing mechanisms
- Disaster recovery to paired region with automated failover strategies
- Cost optimization through serverless analytics, auto-scaling, and resource quotas

## Code Example
```javascript
// Durable Function snippet: policy check and redaction (pseudo-code)
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const tenantId = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  const eventData = req.body;

  // Per-tenant policy validation
  const policy = await getTenantPolicy(tenantId);
  if (!validateEvent(eventData, policy)) {
    context.res = { status: 403, body: 'Policy violation' };
    return;
  }

  // PII redaction
  const redactedData = redactPII(eventData, policy.piiRules);

  // Store to ADLS and trigger downstream processing
  await storeToADLS(tenantId, redactedData);
  await triggerSynapseProcessing(tenantId, redactedData);
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests building an observability-first, Azure-native pipeline with tenant isolation and simple DR, a common beginner-to-intermediate pattern.

## Key Concepts
- Event Hubs, Log Analytics, Azure Monitor, Application Insights
- Delta Lake on ADLS Gen2, per-tenant RBAC
- BYOK via Key Vault, basic DR to paired region
- Cost levers: retention, sampling, tiered storage

## Code Example
```javascript
// publish per-tenant logs to Event Hubs
const { EventHubProducerClient } = require('@azure/event-hubs');
const client = new EventHubProducerClient('<conn>', '<hub>');
async function send(tenantId, payload){
  const batch = await client.createBatch({ partitionKey: tenantId });
  batch.tryAdd(JSON.stringify({ tenantId, payload }));
  await client.sendBatch(batch);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce per-tenant RBAC across API, storage, and analytics views?
- What retention and cost controls would you apply to logs and metrics?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates comprehensive data pipeline design capabilities using Azure's native services, requiring candidates to demonstrate architectural thinking while maintaining accessibility for beginners. It tests understanding of end-to-end data flows, governance principles, and enterprise requirements.

## Key Concepts
- IoT Hub for telemetry ingestion
- Data Lake Storage Gen2 for scalable raw data storage
- Azure Synapse Analytics for data processing and aggregation
- Azure Purview for metadata management and data governance
- Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) for multi-tenant isolation
- Power BI for data visualization and business intelligence
- Bring Your Own Key (BYOK) for enhanced encryption
- Paired region disaster recovery architecture
- Serverless compute and storage tiering for cost optimization

## Code Example
```javascript
module.exports = async function(context, eventHubMessages) {
  // Process incoming telemetry messages
  const telemetryPayloads = eventHubMessages.map(message => 
    JSON.parse(message.getBytes().toString())
  );

  // Persist raw data to Data Lake Gen2
  await dataLakeClient.uploadBatch(telemetryPayloads);

  // Trigger Synapse processing for aggregation
  await synapseClient.invokeStoredProcedure('process_vehicle_aggregates');

  context.log(`Processed ${telemetryPayloads.length} telemetry messages`);
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assess practical knowledge of end-to-end IoT pipelines on Azure, including edge processing, streaming, and lakehouse analytics, plus security and cost controls.

## Key Concepts
- IoT Edge and IoT Hub integration
- Event Hubs as the streaming backbone
- Synapse lakehouse with Delta Lake for per-device isolation
- BYOK via Azure Key Vault; tenant/workspace scoping
- DR across regions and cost levers (retention, autoscale, tiering)

